From 3d2816c243f8db4f4725af99959fcf23a2d91a4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:49:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Round 6: Factor pressure powers out of the Gibbs term
 sums

Group the Region 1 and Region 2 coefficient tables by pressure exponent
at compile time, sum each short reduced-temperature series first and
then scale it by its pressure power. The value and pressure derivative
share one inner sum. This removes about a third of the multiplications
and shortens the serial accumulation chains. Values change in the last
bits; a unit test compares against term-by-term powi sums.

Workload: serial (96 candidates, one worker), matrix API both sides.
Official 11-sample run: 0.273 ms -> 0.256 ms, 1.07x (paired 1.11x).
41-sample confirmation: 0.280 ms -> 0.255 ms, paired 1.11x.
validate.py passed against the release CLI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
